  "raw": " seven months.\n\nBen Saddington, Opposition deputy chief whip and the committee’s Conservative member at this month’s meeting of AMs, said there were also issues with damage to the yard caused by Calgary-based contractor Bison Construction.\n\nHe called on Gareth Morgan, Opposition finance spokesman, to introduce private sector competition between the yard owners if it manages to displace Cardiff. Cardiff continues to accuse its provincial owners of coercion, blackmail, politically motivated abuse of powers and the formation last week of Public Life Wales – itself strongly opposed by Calgary-headquartered Monarch Airlines.\n\nA Cardiff Council spokesperson confirmed: “Senden Farm is an agricultural business and the yard has leases in place with Cardiff Aviation for ten years commencing 2014 to 2024. Cardiff continues dialogue with full co-operation and transparency from all parties involved. Cardiff continues acting openly and transparently and the yard’s overall performance remains consistent with prior periods throughout 2013.”\n\nLast year chief",
  "serialized": "seven months. Ben Saddington, Opposition deputy chief whip and the committee’s Conservative member at this month’s meeting of AMs, said there were also issues with damage to the yard caused by Calgary-based contractor Bison Construction. He called on Gareth Morgan, Opposition finance spokesman, to introduce private sector competition between the yard owners if it manages to displace Cardiff. Cardiff continues to accuse its provincial owners of coercion, blackmail, politically motivated abuse of powers and the formation last week of Public Life Wales – itself strongly opposed by Calgary-headquartered Monarch Airlines. A Cardiff Council spokesperson confirmed: “Senden Farm is an agricultural business and the yard has leases in place with Cardiff Aviation for ten years commencing 2014 to 2024. Cardiff continues dialogue with full co-operation and transparency from all parties involved. Cardiff continues acting openly and transparently and the yard’s overall performance remains consistent with prior periods throughout 2013.” Last year chief",
